\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces The unified benchmark. Each panel's competitive ratios (means over paired trials; every 95\% CI $\le 0.003$) sit beside their bar chart (error bars: 95\% CIs; dashed line: advice-free floor; dotted: oracle ceiling). Bold marks the worst column of each unguarded prediction-follower; all three fall below their own panel's floor. That floor is instance-dependent --- it is Ranking's ratio on that panel's graph family, not a constant --- so the three floors ($0.948$, $0.890$, $0.990$) are not comparable with one another, and neither are the quality columns across the two prediction families (\S  3.3).}}{20}{table.4.1}\protected@file@percent }
