\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.4}{\ignorespaces The testing-wall frontier. Horizontal axis: baseline strength \(\rho _{\mathrm  {base}}\), swept by the number of request types (weaker baseline and larger \(r\) to the left). Vertical axis: consistency upside over the baseline. As the baseline weakens, the \emph  {potential} upside of perfect advice grows, but the upside a sublinear test can \emph  {safely capture} stays near zero, because the empirical test's resolution sits far above the break-even margin wherever the upside exists.}}{30}{figure.6.4}\protected@file@percent }
